% toy-branch.ill — tiny branching machine for the CALC book chapter 10.
%
% A coin-flip machine: toss a flip token and handle both outcomes.
% The toss rule produces (heads + tails) — oplus: the system commits to
% one branch. explore (symex) follows BOTH; exec follows ONE (committed choice).

flip: type.
heads: type.
tails: type.
prize: type.
bust: type.

% toss: consume flip, produce EITHER heads OR tails (system decides).
toss: flip -o { heads + tails }.

% Two continuations, one per branch.
win:  heads -o { prize }.
lose: tails -o { bust }.

#symex flip .
